  "limitations": [
    "Portable SIMD schedule and scalar rounds do not use optional CPU SHA instructions; the independent detected-feature reference is substantially faster.",
    "Small-input digest pipelines still allocate and are slower than the independent portable fallback.",
    "Immutable checkpoints, fresh digest buffers and owned stream chunks have different allocation behavior from mutable reference states.",
    "Foreign kernels were compiled to objects but were not executed.",
    "A runtime-size identity keeps large constant fixture setup out of the Rust checker after constant evaluation overflowed its stack; that compiler limitation is not claimed fixed.",
    "Native wide closures, wide tail groups and public wide primitive object exports retain the restrictions recorded by the compiler prerequisite. The library uses private wide schedule primitives and ordinary-word state loops."
